<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ouadane</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ouadane is an oasis town in the Adrar region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>, founded in the 12th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> traders on the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. It prospered on the caravan trade in salt, gold and dates, and the Portuguese set up a short-lived trading post there in the late 15th century. Its stone-built old town and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> libraries are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ouadane.jpg" alt="Ouadane" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clemens Schmillen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OuadaneOldTown1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
